  "narrative": "Synthesis of the H100 response deadline. H100 tests CDKN2A loss versus CDKN2A-intact lines for MDM2 dependency within TP53-loss lines; direction -1, so a positive signed estimate denotes a more negative MDM2 score, i.e. stronger dependency. Discovery R69 was +0.111 (95% CI +0.035 to +0.186), above my working practical threshold, but the independent validation R105 was only +0.083 with an independent interval from -0.018 to +0.183 at the run-wide multiplicity-adjusted alpha. The validation interval crosses zero and the point estimate is below the threshold, so the new evidence does not confirm the TP53-loss subgroup claim. I keep H100 unresolved and close the exact original comparison rather than accept or reject it. The broader CDKN2A loss-MDM2 association remains accepted: H94 overall R62 +0.117 (CI +0.082 to +0.152), independently validated by R78 +0.130 (independent interval +0.075 to +0.185); TP53-wildtype H99, MTAP-wildtype H110, and high screen-QC H105 also support the general association. H100 leaves only the context-specific question of persistence in TP53-loss lines unresolved, with current evidence suggesting possible attenuation but not establishing absence. Supported dataset associations, after independent validation where available, are: TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency (H7: R7 +0.802, CI +0.782 to +0.822; R92 +0.790, independent interval +0.761 to +0.819; context H16/H44/H50/H73), KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H13: R9 +0.796, CI +0.776 to +0.816; R26 +0.806, independent interval +0.775 to +0.838), SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H10: R10 +0.784, CI +0.765 to +0.803; R39 +0.793, independent interval +0.763 to +0.822; contexts H31/H58/H74), MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency (H8: R8 +0.790, CI +0.760 to +0.819; R52 +0.802, independent interval +0.753 to +0.851; contexts H32/H75), PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency (H67: R55 +0.267, CI +0.215 to +0.319; R65 +0.329, independent interval +0.255 to +0.402; contexts H96/H97/H104), and CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency overall (H94). These are associations in the supplied lung-cell-line dataset, not causal claims or claims of external generalizability. The main negative/specificity findings are also substantive. Driver/RTK and pathway probes mostly show no practical dependency-score differences: KRAS mutation, BRAF V600E, NF1 loss, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, APC, STK11, SMAD4, MYC, RB1, and many other markers were near or exactly null for the tested dependencies. Cross-pathway tests showed that KEAP1 loss did not extend to SMARCA2, SMARCA4 loss did not extend to USP7 or POLR2A, TP53 loss did not extend to WRN or NFE2L2, and PTEN loss did not extend to MDM2 in TP53-wildtype lines. This makes the accepted associations more biologically specific rather than suggesting broad p53, NRF2, SWI/SNF, or RTK-bypass effects. H128 is a small, borderline, opposite-direction finding after broad exploration and is not treated as a new meaningful effect. Most informative next analysis: I registered a refinement of H100 that asks whether CDKN2A loss versus MDM2 dependency persists within TP53-loss AND MTAP-wildtype cells, reducing possible CDKN2A/MTAP co-loss confounding. If that clean context is imprecise or below about 0.1, close the TP53-loss context as unsupported; if a robust signal appears, revise the context-specific interpretation. Future validation should be reserved for a newly discovered primary association of at least practical size with an interval away from zero, not for small or opposite-direction probes.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis ledger summary. Core accepted/validated: TP53 loss weak USP7 (H7/R7/R92); KEAP1 loss weak NFE2L2 (H13/R9/R26); SMARCA4 loss strong SMARCA2 (H10/R10/R39); MSI-high strong WRN (H8/R8/R52); PTEN loss strong STAT3 (H67/R55/R65); CDKN2A loss strong MDM2 overall (H94/R62/R78, contexts H99/H110/H105). H100 TP53-loss CDKN2A-MDM2 unresolved/closed: R69 discovery +0.111, R105 validation +0.083 crossing zero and below threshold; keep unresolved, propose refinement with tp53_loss=1 and mtap_loss=0 to test co-loss confounding. Negative panel: no meaningful MAPK/RTK, MYC, APC/STK11/SMAD4/NF1/RB1 effects; specificity accepted. No causal/generalizability claims. Validation budget reserved."
